WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.534
-You are here.
It is a great day

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.968
to be in New York City.
Well, unless you're one person.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:12.934
Today, history was made today
in New York City

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:15.868
as former president Trump
became the first U.S. president

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:18.934
to ever be arrested
and face criminal charges.

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:24.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:25.634
When they heard,
New Yorkers were like,

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:26.834
-♪ It's about damn time ♪

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:29.968
-Yeah. Uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:31.601
Trump made history.

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.200
The only good news for Trump,
in Florida,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.734
all the history books
have been thrown out.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.667
So it's all right.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:38.968
Meanwhile, on his way to court,

00:00:38.968 --> 00:00:41.667
Trump posted on social media
from the car.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.801
He wrote,
"Heading to Lower Manhattan,

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.367
the courthouse.
Seems so surreal.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.467
Wow, they are
going to arrest me.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:49.734
Can't believe this
is happening in America.

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:52.133
MAGA!"
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.467
When Trump sits in the back

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.868
of a car,
he's like a little kid.

00:00:54.868 --> 00:00:56.434
You've got to give him
a bag of Cheerios and an iPad.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:58.767
It's like, "We'll be
at court soon, honey."

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.400
Trump eventually
reached the courthouse.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.968
Here he is walking in.

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:05.200
-...outside his vehicle,

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.901
once they have a handle
of the security here.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:09.400
And then you see
the former president...

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:12.100
-Gave a little wave there.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.400
Gave a little wa--

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.300
Can we -- who is --
Can we see who he's waving at?

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.167
-...once they have a handle
of the security here.

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:19.467
And then you see
the former president...

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.767
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, wow.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.267
[ Applause ]

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.634
That is biz-- That is --

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:25.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
The odds --

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.868
The odds of that happening.
The odds of that happening.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:31.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.334
Wow.

00:01:33.334 --> 00:01:34.434
Well, once he was inside,

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:36.667
Trump was booked
and fingerprinted.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.467
If you want to know
what his fingerprints look like,

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.100
just look at
a "Don't walk" sign.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.300
Yep, Trump was actually
fingerprinted.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.734
They didn't even use an ink pad.

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.868
They just used the McRib sauce
that was already on his fingers.

00:01:48.868 --> 00:01:53.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.534
Once he got inside
the courtroom,

00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:56.801
Trump was formally charged
with 34 counts

00:01:56.801 --> 00:02:00.133
of falsifying business records
in the first degree,

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.601
which are class E felonies.

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:05.701
Yep, Trump was like, "Of course,
they were very classy felonies."

00:02:05.701 --> 00:02:07.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.334 --> 00:02:09.534
"Some would say
the classiest of felonies."

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:10.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:12.133
If this goes to trial,

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:15.868
prosecutors plan to call
Stormy Daniels as a witness.

00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:17.367
-Stormy Daniels!
-Stormy Daniels -- Yeah.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:18.634
Stormy Daniels heard
and was like,

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:19.934
"Haven't I witnessed enough?"

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:25.334
Here's a picture of Trump
inside the courtroom.

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:26.767
Ooh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:28.868
He looks like he's watching
another table at Applebee's

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.100
get their food first.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:36.267
Could we see him again?
That face?

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:38.901
Yeah. He looks...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.901 --> 00:02:41.834
Looks like he had to sit through
two unskippable ads on YouTube.

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:44.701
Let me just see it
one more time.

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:48.434
He looks like Ben Affleck
at the Grammys.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.567
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:51.968
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:53.234
Meanwhile, earlier today,

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:55.701
Marjorie Taylor Greene
and George Santos

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:57.400
both showed up
outside the courthouse,

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.367
and it was absolute chaos.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:01.634
It was basically the craziest
Thanksgiving Day Parade.

00:03:01.634 --> 00:03:03.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.667
Even Times Square Elmo was like,

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.934
"If they try to engage,
just walk right past them.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.534
Don't even --
Don't engage with the --"

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:09.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.501
Yeah.
But as soon as George Santos

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:12.868
showed up outside
the courthouse,

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:15.367
he was swarmed by reporters.
Take a look at this photo.

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:18.601
Yeah. Trump saw the media
following Santos, was like,

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:20.300
"Hey, get your own arraignment!"

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.634
Marjorie Taylor Greene
was then interviewed

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:25.734
about Trump's indictment,

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:27.133
and she made
an interesting comparison.

00:03:27.133 --> 00:03:28.634
Listen to this.
-I mean, think about --

00:03:28.634 --> 00:03:30.133
Gosh, think about this.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:33.701
President Trump is joining some
of the most incredible people

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.200
in history,
being arrested today.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.400
Nelson Mandela was arrested,
served time in prison.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.601
Jesus.
Jesus was arrested.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:49.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:52.234
-Jesus -- Jesus saw that
and said, "Jesus..."

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:53.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:55.234
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:55.234 --> 00:04:01.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.133
Yeah, it was a long day
of media coverage,

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:05.167
with reporters starting
early in the morning

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.067
and talking nonstop
about the case.

00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:08.400
I admire their dedication,

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.167
but I think some of them
need to take a break.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.367
Check out this clip
I saw earlier today on CNN.

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:14.334
-[ Hoarsely ] After the search
warrant at Mar-a-Lago,

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:15.534
he raised a million dollars.

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:17.667
After being indicted,
he raised $7 million.

00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.501
-[ Hoarsely ] We do know that
there's a videographer

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:20.834
along with him right now.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.434
-[ Hoarsely ] It's not that
out of the ordinary

00:04:22.434 --> 00:04:24.467
to ask for a change in venue.

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.234
Staten Island, I think,
went majority for Trump,

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.567
so no wonder he's trying
to get over there again.

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:29.767
-[ Laughs hoarsely ]

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:33.067
-Get a little water,
something.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:35.634
[ Applause ]

00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:37.767
Need a little water.

00:04:37.767 --> 00:04:39.400
Oh, and I saw that
Senator Lindsey Graham

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.501
said Trump's indictment
almost ensures

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:44.901
that he will be
the 2024 Republican nominee.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.734
But now several other members
of Congress

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:48.267
are speaking out
about the situation.

00:04:48.267 --> 00:04:50.234
For example,
Senator Mark Kelly said...

00:04:55.267 --> 00:04:56.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:58.300
Then Congressman
Jack Bergman said...

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:06.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:08.133
And Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene said...

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:12.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.400
Then Congressman Raul Ruiz
said...

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.100
Then Senator Tom Cotton said...

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:36.601
Congressman Brad Sherman said...

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:40.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:52.167
Congressman George Santos
said...

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:54.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.934 --> 00:06:01.067
Then Congresswoman
Chellie Pingree said...

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:04.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:09.601
Then Congressman Richard Neal
said...

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:12.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.133
And finally,
Senator Mark Kelly said...

00:06:18.467 --> 00:06:19.767
[ Laughter ]
There you go.

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.801
Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

